# AI Configuration for NEXA Project

## Local AI (Ollama) - RECOMMENDED 🌟

### 1. Install Ollama
```bash
# Windows (Chocolatey)
choco install ollama

# Linux (Ubuntu/Debian)
curl -fsSL https://ollama.ai/install.sh | sh

# macOS (Homebrew)
brew install --cask ollama
```

### 2. Pull Models
```bash
ollama pull llama3.2        # Default model
ollama pull mistral         # Alternative
ollama pull gemma           # Another option
```

### 3. Configure Environment (optional)
No need - auto-detection works! Just ensure Ollama is running:
```bash
# Start Ollama service
ollama serve
```

## Cloud API (OpenAI/Azure) - Fallback Option

### For OpenAI API:
1. Get your API key from https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
2. Set environment variable in backend/.env.local or .env file:
   ```bash
   OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-key-here
   # Optional URL override (default is openAI)
   OPENAI_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions
   ```

### For Azure OpenAI:
```bash
AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://your-resource-name.openai.azure.com/
AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=your-azure-key-here
AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT_NAME=gpt-35-turbo-deployment
```

## Environment Variables Reference

| Variable | Description | Example | Required? |
|----------|-------------|---------|-----------|
| `OLLAMA_ENABLED` | Enable Ollama local AI | true/false | No (auto-detects) |
| `OPENAI_API_KEY` | OpenAI API key | sk-... | No (uses mock if missing) |
| `OPENAI_URL` | Custom API endpoint | https://... | No |
| `AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT` | Azure resource URL | ...openai.azure.com/ | No |
| `AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY` | Azure API key | eyJhbGci... | No |

## Auto-Detection Flow

1. **Start Backend** → Check for Ollama running at localhost:11434
2. **Found Ollama?** ✅ → Use llama3.2 by default (FREE, PRIVATE)
3. **No Ollama?** ⚠️ → Check environment variables
4. **API Keys found?** ✅ → Use OpenAI/Azure
5. **No keys?** ❌ → System works without AI (mock responses)

## Quick Test

After starting backend:
```bash
# API endpoint to check status
GET http://localhost:3001/api/chat/status
```

Expected response with Ollama running:
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "providers": [
      {
        "name": "Ollama Local",
        "type": "local-llm",
        "status": "active"
      }
    ],
    "availableModels": ["llama3.2:latest"]
  }
}
```
